A||N||2||Elenor84||Inner Tie rod replacement.||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||12-02-2000||03:50 AM||||Hey guys, I just bought inner tie rod for my right side...how do I go about replacing it?  Do I have to do a wheel alignment afterwards?  And how do I do that?<BR>Thx alot!<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||12-02-2000||10:01 AM||||Unfortunately, the inner tie rod is somewhat of a pain in the hinny to replace. You're "supposed" to use a special inner tie rod tool, but it can be done without it too, if you have a well equiped toolbox. You are also supposed to have it aligned after any tie rod work. An alignment shop has to do that, no other way around it. If you carefully count the number of rotations as you unscrew the tie rod, and put the new one back on exactly the same, you "might" get away without an alignment. Search past posts for more details, this has been discussed before.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||12-02-2000||04:13 PM||||Thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||10
